he ballot after losing renomination, Democrat James Talarico faces scandal-prone Attorney General Ken Paxton. Recent polls give Talarico a narrow lead, ranging from tied to six points, with averages clustering around three points. Prediction markets price Talarico's chances near 60 to 64 percent.\n\nThe race has tightened in recent days. Talarico's 12-day absence from campaigning with the flu has drawn attacks from Trump and Paxton, and some coverage suggests momentum may be shifting toward Republicans as early voting nears. Paxton also faces friction within his own party, complaining publicly about lacking Cornyn's support. Money strongly favors Talarico, who has raised nearly $69 million and holds a large cash advantage, while outside groups have spent heavily against Paxton. The race remains genuinely competitive but leans Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7008, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6832, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7125, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7022, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.6}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6724, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6815, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6849, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6371, "margin": 2.3}]}